# CODEOWNERS: platform-enforced split between safe and sensitive paths.
#
# With branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners" (and required
# approvals: 0), an owner on a path means that pull requests touching it need
# a human approval before merge. Only pull requests where *every* file is
# ownerless can merge without an approver.
#
# Sensitive by default: everything has a human owner, and safe paths are
# explicit exceptions. A new path is therefore sensitive until someone
# deliberately adds it to the exceptions. The last match wins, so the order
# below matters:
#   1. the default owner for everything
#   2. safe exceptions (lines without an owner remove the requirement)
#   3. sensitive files inside the safe exceptions
#   4. areas with another owner (agentctl/sandbox), which override all of the above

# 1. Default: everything needs review, including paths that do not exist yet
*                             @olebhansen

# 2. Safe paths: documentation that is neither built into images, read as
#    agent instructions nor changes dependencies
/README.md
/LICENSE
/docs/
/agents/*/README.md
/integrations/README.md

# 3. Sensitive files inside the safe paths: dependencies
#    (docs/presentations/ has its own package.json files)
package.json                  @olebhansen
package-lock.json             @olebhansen

# 4. The agent layer moved in from altinn-studio (ki-lab) is owned by its team.
#    Listed last so these paths do not need the default owner, and vice versa.
/agentctl/                    @martinothamar
/sandbox/                     @martinothamar
/images/agentctl-base/        @martinothamar
/docker-bake.hcl              @martinothamar
# The Rust workspace at the root and the agentctl/sandbox workflows
/Cargo.toml                   @martinothamar
/Cargo.lock                   @martinothamar
/rust-toolchain.toml          @martinothamar
/rustfmt.toml                 @martinothamar
/clippy.toml                  @martinothamar
/deny.toml                    @martinothamar
/Makefile                     @martinothamar
/.cargo/                      @martinothamar
/.editorconfig                @martinothamar
/.github/workflows/rust.yml   @martinothamar
/.github/workflows/agentctl-*.yml @martinothamar
# The agentctl agent that develops the platform itself
/agents/self-dev/             @martinothamar
